WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.700
Welcome back, champ!

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:17.130
Last time: 101 → 4 + 0 + 1 = 5

3
00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:24.110
Chapter 2 · Odd, Even, and Patterns

4
00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:31.550
Share, hop, and clap!

5
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:41.650
Riya shares laddoos: two on every plate

6
00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:52.060
8 laddoos → 4 pairs, none left over

7
00:00:52.060 --> 00:01:02.470
7 laddoos → 3 pairs and 1 left over

8
00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:12.760
Why is one laddoo left over? Think!

9
00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:19.770
Two kinds of numbers. Let's name them!

10
00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:29.740
EVEN: makes pairs, nothing left over

11
00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:39.890
ODD: one left over

12
00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:45.890
Every whole number is odd OR even

13
00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:53.210
Pairs test: make pairs, see what's left

14
00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:59.400
6 → 3 pairs, none left → EVEN

15
00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:05.350
9 → 4 pairs + 1 left → ODD

16
00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:13.390
11 → 5 pairs + 1 left → ODD

17
00:02:13.390 --> 00:02:23.570
Big number? Just look at the last digit!

18
00:02:23.570 --> 00:02:29.540
Ends in 0, 2, 4, 6, 8 → EVEN

19
00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:34.660
Ends in 1, 3, 5, 7, 9 → ODD

20
00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:42.650
38 ends in 8 → even · 25 ends in 5 → odd

21
00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:53.480
Tens always make pairs, so the last digit decides

22
00:02:53.480 --> 00:03:00.500
1 to 20: odd in orange, even in green

23
00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:14.220
Odd, even, odd, even… they take turns!

24
00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:22.890
How many odd numbers from 1 to 10?

25
00:03:22.890 --> 00:03:34.400
Five! 1, 3, 5, 7, 9

26
00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:43.550
Tinku the frog skips every other number

27
00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:53.230
Start at 2: 2, 4, 6, 8, 10 → evens

28
00:03:53.230 --> 00:04:02.710
Start at 1: 1, 3, 5, 7, 9 → odds

29
00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:12.000
Start at 1… will Tinku land on 20?

30
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:23.350
No! 20 is even. He lands on 19, then 21

31
00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:31.790
The rule: add 2 each time

32
00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:40.210
2, 4, 6, 8, ___?

33
00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.580
10! 8 + 2 = 10

34
00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:51.770
10, 12, 14, ___?

35
00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:57.980
16! 14 + 2 = 16

36
00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:09.290
A pattern repeats by a rule: clap, snap…

37
00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:16.920
Clap, snap, clap, snap, clap, ___?

38
00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:22.360
Snap! They take turns, like odd and even

39
00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:37.940
Clap on the even numbers: 2, 4, 6, 8

40
00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:46.370
Code loves rules that repeat!

41
00:05:46.370 --> 00:06:00.210
7, 12, 15, 20, 3, 18: which are even?

42
00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:12.030
Even: 12, 20, 18 · Odd: 7, 15, 3

43
00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:15.730
Your turn: practice check

44
00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:25.370
Is 14 odd or even? How do you know?

45
00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:35.880
Even! 7 pairs, none left over, ends in 4

46
00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:41.240
Even = pairs, nothing left over

47
00:06:41.240 --> 00:06:43.990
Odd = one left over

48
00:06:43.990 --> 00:06:50.300
Last digit 0, 2, 4, 6, 8 → even

49
00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:54.970
Patterns repeat by a rule

50
00:06:54.970 --> 00:07:02.890
Chapter 2 done!

51
00:07:02.890 --> 00:07:09.690
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
